# The holding(..) clause of a signature seeds, in Link, the contents of the object that the built-in allocates. The proven level reads no contents from the type of the container itself.
# Where Link's claim gives a read its type, the walk emits a check after the read in every build.
# Fault injection, testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Object.keys/ContentsOfResult: Object.keys() is assumed to return an array that holds only null.
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: string
# CHECK-NEXT: went on
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Object.keys/ContentsOfResult
# LIE: found string in an element
# LIE-NOT: went on
# LIE: crashed
